              "marks": 4,
              "answer": "2 marks each:\n(i) Internal economies of scale are the cost advantages a firm gains from increasing its own size or scale of production, which cause its average cost per unit to fall.\n(ii) Internal diseconomies of scale are the disadvantages a firm faces when it grows too large, which cause its average cost per unit to rise (for example poor communication and management problems)."
